    "title": "Sum Root to Leaf Numbers",
    "workload": "build 4 balanced 2047-node trees once, then 40000 full root-to-leaf DFS traversals. Depth is bounded on purpose: each path spells a base-10 number so a depth-18 tree overflows i64 outright and kara traps overflow, aborting rather than measuring; at depth 11 the leaf sum stays near 1e14. The punch count carries the workload instead. NOTE: this is the corpus's only shared-struct (RC) tree kata -- kara and the Rust mirror (Rc) both pay retain/release traffic during the traversal, while Go (GC pointers) and C (raw malloc'd pointers) do not. kara's RC-elision optimization is worth 34.6% here, measured by rebuilding with KARAC_RC_ELIDE_REF_PARAMS=0.",
